    "notes": {
        "6bec247e-d0ef-4332-9383-93dce671e010": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 560,
            "width": 736,
            "height": 320,
            "content": "## Test data assumption: one real Nuki device\n\nNuki has no sandbox. The connected account (API token with the scopes smartlock.readOnly, smartlock.action, smartlock.auth and smartlock.log) must hold at least one Smart Lock that is online. The flow takes the first device Find Smartlocks returns, so no device ID is hardcoded.\n\nA **Nuki Keypad** must be paired with that device, and for short-term rental accounts the device needs an active Smart Hosting subscription (otherwise Nuki answers 402).\n\nCreate Keypad Code waits until Nuki Web lists the new code (up to 5 minutes), so the After All timeout is 480 s. The \"notConfirmed\" port is left open on purpose: when the code never appears the flow times out and fails. The 1-minute Wait gives the device time to take the update; do not remove it. Delete Smartlock Authorization removes the code again. If a run is aborted, delete the authorization named \"E2E <timestamp>\" in Nuki Web."
        }
    }
}
